Let $t\ge 3$ be an integer and $I_1,\ldots,I_t\subseteq[n]$ be subsets satisfying
  \begin{enumerate}
\item [\rm{(i)}] ${\rm wt}(I_J)\leq (|J|-1)k$ for all  nonempty $J\subseteq [t]$,
\item [\rm{(ii)}] Equality holds for $J=[t]$, i.e., ${\rm wt}(I_{[t]})=(t-1)k$.
  \end{enumerate}
  Then the $t$-wise intersection matrix $M_{k,(I_1,\ldots,I_t)}$ is nonsingular over any finite field.
